Thus ends the twenty-fourth chapter in the Śukla Yajurveda Kāṇva Saṃhitā.

223.m:
You are taken with a support; I take you pleasing to Prajāpati. This is your womb; the sun is your greatness.
The greatness of yours that arose in the year, by day; the greatness of yours that arose in Vāyu, in mid-air;
the greatness of yours that arose in heaven, in the sun: to that greatness of yours, to Prajāpati, svāhā! To the gods!

224.m:
You are taken with a support; I take you pleasing to Prajāpati. This is your womb; the moon is your greatness.
The greatness of yours that arose in the year, by night; the greatness of yours that arose on earth, in Agni;
the greatness of yours that arose in the stars, in the moon: to that greatness of yours, to Prajāpati, to the gods, svāhā!

226.m:
Agni was the animal: with him they sacrificed. He won this world where Agni is;
that world will be yours, you will win it: drink these waters.
Vāyu was the animal: with him they sacrificed. He won this world where Vāyu is;
that world will be yours, you will win it: drink these waters.
The sun was the animal: with him they sacrificed. He won this world where the sun is;
that world will be yours, you will win it: drink these waters.
